// tap-echo: --buffer 65535 --close-after 0
// SYN+FIN parses now (RFC 9293 does not forbid the combination). Linux's tcp_v4_rcv
// end_seq computation counts SYN and FIN as one sequence octet each (tcp_ipv4.c:2162-2163,
// end_seq = seq + th->syn + th->fin + len), and tcp_timewait_state_process
// (tcp_minisocks.c:99-263) never branches on th->fin on its own: a SYN+FIN at or before
// RCV.NXT fails the reopen-candidate test the same way a lone SYN would and falls to the
// generic out-of-window ACK (tcp_minisocks.c:248-259, tcp_timewait_check_oow_rate_limit).
// Zhida: wire/tcp.rs Repr::parse accepts SYN+FIN as Control::SynFin, two octets of
// sequence space (matching Linux's end_seq math); socket/tcp.rs process() routes it
// through the same TIME-WAIT SYN path as Control::Syn (time_wait_accepts_syn,
// challenge_ack_reply).
// Ensure that the reception of a TCP SYN with SEG.SEQ = RCV.NXT - 1
// in the TIME-WAIT state does not affect the TCP connection.
// Adapted from freebsd-net/tcp-testsuite commit 04b8c73fc5081fe3792f1bed9168c9b22aaedddb,
// state-event-engine/rcv-syn-fin-time-wait/rcv-syn-fin-time-wait-using-shutdown-outside-left-secure-drop-ipv4.pkt
// (BSD-2-Clause; notice below). Changes for Zhida's packet-only runner, tap-echo
// being the application (fuzz/packetdrill/README.md, "Upstream suites"):
// - IPv4 variant. Dropped: sysctls, which set FreeBSD defaults and
//   net.inet.tcp.drop_synfin=1 (SYN|FIN dropped, as Linux drops it in LISTEN) and
//   net.inet.tcp.insecure_syn=0 (RFC 5961 SYN checks on); Zhida has no such switch;
//   fcntl; getsockopt(SO_RCVBUF); --tolerance_usecs=75000 (the runner keeps
//   packetdrill's 4 ms); sockstat and tcpdrop commands except where replaced below.
// - socket/bind/listen/accept dropped: tap-echo listens on port 8080 and accepts.
// - shutdown(SHUT_WR) becomes tap-echo --close-after 0: Zhida sends its FIN right
//   after the handshake (upstream: 0.1 s later).
// - Receive window: tap-echo --buffer 65535, so Zhida's RCV.WND is 65535, its
//   advertised window (no window scale), as upstream's.
// - Upstream's #ifdef STANDARD branch kept (the RFC expectation); its #ifdef FreeBSD
//   branch, FreeBSD's own behavior, dropped.
// - Still in TIME-WAIT (upstream: sockstat 0.1 s after the event): 1.1 s after the
//   event the client retransmits its FIN and Zhida ACKs it; a closed connection
//   would leave a listener, which answers RST. 1.1 s, not 0.1 s: Zhida sends at
//   most one ACK per second to out-of-window segments without payload (smoltcp
//   0.14.0 src/socket/tcp.rs 1545-1550, 1821-1830; Linux limits them to one per
//   0.5 s), and the event may have drawn one.
//
